You need to take into account that the ray is rotated 480 degrees in a clockwise direction.
480 is 12 full rotations for clockwise (\(12 \times 360\) degrees). Hence the ray will still be pointing at the same position as it was initially.
To know the measure of the angle, consider the below figure.
[asy]
draw((0,0)--dir(40),linewidth(1),Arrow);
draw((0,0)--dir(0),linewidth(1),Arrow);
dot(.8dir(40));
dot(.8dir(0));
dot((0,0));
label("A",.8dir(40),NW);
label("B",.8dir(0),S);
label("C",(0,0),W);
draw((0,0)--1.5dir(40),linewidth(1));
extend((0,0)--1.5dir(40),Arrow);
[/asy]
The angle between \(C, A,\) and \(B\) remains 40o. Also, the angle between \(C, B,\) and \(A\) remains 40 degrees.
Thus, the angle \(ACB\) is 40 degrees.
[/think]
ooter <answer>$$40$$</answer>

